---
// Manifesto: site.md §2, copy verbatim. The title stands where every page has it (label above, left edge); below it
// the principles run down the right. Each principle's number stands in the left column in Lead at a third of the ink and stays in view while its
// principle is read (sticky), so the column carries the structure, not just the page label.
// Two pacings, set on <main> (both kept for review until one is chosen):
//   data-pace="length": the pause after a principle grows with its length (data-len on the article);
//   data-pace="screen": one principle, one screen (from 900px wide; the phone keeps even gaps).
// data-italic="whose" | "typing" | "purpose": the italic switch (brand: one anomaly per composition) on one word of the
// explanations; without it, no switch. Georgia stands in for the anomaly face until web fonts exist.
import Site from "../layouts/Site.astro";
---

<Site title="Manifesto" description="Five principles I work by." image="/review-og.png">
  <main class="page manifesto" data-pace="length">
    <!-- The title in the one place every page has it: the label over it, both at the left edge (site.css .page-title). -->
    <section class="part intro">
      <h1 class="label caps">MANIFESTO</h1>
      <p class="page-title">Five principles I work&nbsp;by.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- The articles take the row's own columns (subgrid), so the numbers line up with the label above them. -->
    <section class="row principles">
      <article data-len="long">
        <div class="side"><span class="num">01.</span></div>
        <div class="text">
          <h2>Every decision has an&nbsp;author.</h2>
          <p>If no one will defend it, it shouldn't ship. Every product is built on a few thousand small decisions: what the cancel button says, where the password strength meter sits, whether the empty state is funny or quiet. Most of those get made by accident. I make them on&nbsp;<span class="sw" data-w="purpose">purpose</span>.</p>
          <p>Settings are unfinished decisions. So is sending people to support for something the screen could have told them. "Make it customizable" is what designers say when they can't&nbsp;decide.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article data-len="short">
        <div class="side"><span class="num">02.</span></div>
        <div class="text">
          <h2>The brief is wrong until proven&nbsp;right.</h2>
          <p>A brief is the founder's first guess at the problem. The work starts with checking that guess. If you hand me a brief and I do exactly what it says, I'm not designing. I'm&nbsp;<span class="sw" data-w="typing">typing</span>.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article data-len="short">
        <div class="side"><span class="num">03.</span></div>
        <div class="text">
          <h2>Make the call, then check&nbsp;it.</h2>
          <p>Research sharpens a decision. It doesn't replace one. I decide from what I've seen, and research where I'm&nbsp;unsure.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article data-len="mid">
        <div class="side"><span class="num">04.</span></div>
        <div class="text">
          <h2>Character is not a&nbsp;layer.</h2>
          <p>A product has one voice or none. The voice shows up in places people don't think of as design: the wording on a 404, the timing of a toast notification, what your invoice email feels like. If those don't match the rest of the product, the product doesn't have a voice. It has a&nbsp;styleguide.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article data-len="mid">
        <div class="side"><span class="num">05.</span></div>
        <div class="text">
          <h2>The safe version is already&nbsp;taken.</h2>
          <p>Every category has its safe version, and it's already taken. The banking app in navy blue. The pharmacy site that opens with a sale. Building another one puts you at the back of a line someone else started. You should be able to tell <span class="sw" data-w="whose">whose</span> product it is without seeing the&nbsp;logo.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="row">
      <span class="label" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <div class="end">
        <hr class="rule" />
        <div class="closing">
          <p>If this sounds like how you want to build —</p>
          <a class="btn" href="/review/" data-gem>Send a link, get a video review <span class="arw">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Site>

<!-- Review toggles for the variants: /manifesto/?pace=screen, ?italic=whose (or typing, purpose). Remove together with
     the variants that aren't chosen. -->
<script is:inline>
  (() => {
    const q = new URLSearchParams(location.search);
    const main = document.querySelector("main.manifesto");
    if (!main) return;
    if (q.get("pace")) main.dataset.pace = q.get("pace");
    if (q.get("italic")) main.dataset.italic = q.get("italic");
  })();
</script>

<style>
  .intro {
    gap: 20px;
    padding-top: 40px;
  }

  /* The pause after a principle, by its length: two paragraphs, one long paragraph, one short. After the last one the
     page's own step leads to the closing. */
  article {
    --rest: 120px;
  }
  article[data-len="long"] {
    --rest: 200px;
  }
  article[data-len="mid"] {
    --rest: 160px;
  }
  article:last-child {
    --rest: 0px;
  }

  .principles {
    row-gap: 0;
  }
  /* The pause is padding on the article, outside its one grid row: the number's cell is only as tall as the text. */
  article {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: subgrid;
    align-content: start;
    align-items: start;
    padding-bottom: var(--rest);
  }
  /* The number's cell stretches to the text's row only: a sticky grid item would be held by the whole article, pause
     included, so the number sticks inside this cell instead. */
  .side {
    align-self: stretch;
  }
  /* The number, in the left column: as large as the title, a third of the ink. It stays 96px from the top while its
     text goes by, from the title down to the last line, and leaves with it. */
  .num {
    display: block;
    position: sticky;
    top: 96px;
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    opacity: 0.3;
  }
  .text {
    display: grid;
    gap: 16px;
    max-width: 36em;
  }
  h2 {
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  /* 28.5em keeps the longest line at 70 characters (brand: 55–70); at 29em the 04 paragraph reaches 72. */
  .text p {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 28.5em;
    line-height: 1.5;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  /* One principle, one screen: each takes most of a screen, so the next title only shows at the bottom. A long
     principle still keeps a pause after it. */
  @media (min-width: 901px) {
    .manifesto[data-pace="screen"] article {
      box-sizing: border-box;
      min-height: 72vh;
      padding-bottom: 96px;
    }
    .manifesto[data-pace="screen"] article:last-child {
      min-height: 0;
      padding-bottom: 0;
    }
  }

  /* The italic switch: one word, in the anomaly face, at zero tracking. */
  .manifesto[data-italic="whose"] .sw[data-w="whose"],
  .manifesto[data-italic="typing"] .sw[data-w="typing"],
  .manifesto[data-italic="purpose"] .sw[data-w="purpose"] {
    font-family: var(--font-anomaly);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 1.06em;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: 0;
  }

  .end {
    display: grid;
    gap: 64px;
  }

  /* One column: the number sits above its title, as the label sits above the page title; the text takes the full
     width. The pauses keep their order at about half the size; one screen each makes no sense here, so even gaps. */
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    article {
      row-gap: 6px;
    }
    article {
      padding-bottom: calc(24px + var(--rest) * 0.4);
    }
    .num {
      position: static;
    }
    .manifesto[data-pace="screen"] article {
      padding-bottom: 88px;
    }
    article:last-child,
    .manifesto[data-pace="screen"] article:last-child {
      padding-bottom: 0;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .intro {
      padding-top: 16px;
    }
    .num,
    h2 {
      font-size: 24px;
    }
    .end {
      gap: 48px;
    }
  }
</style>
